# Keep the Python side out of the Vercel build.
#
# `legacy/` is the Streamlit app (deployed separately, on Render) and most of `scripts/`
# only runs on your machine or in CI to regenerate public/data/league.json. Neither is
# needed to build or serve the Next.js app, and excluding them keeps the upload small and
# stops Vercel's framework detection from noticing Python it should not act on.
#
# NOTE: public/data/league.json IS required at build time — do not exclude public/.
#
# scripts/ensure-dist.mjs is the ONE exception: it's `prebuild` in package.json, an npm
# lifecycle hook that runs before every `npm run build` regardless of platform, Vercel
# included. Excluding the whole scripts/ folder made Vercel's build fail outright —
# `Cannot find module '/vercel/path0/scripts/ensure-dist.mjs'` — because npm tries to run
# the hook before the build even starts. The script itself already no-ops off Windows
# (`process.env.VERCEL` check), so shipping it costs nothing; it just has to be THERE.
legacy/
scripts/*.py
scripts/__pycache__/
Old Models/
*.pyc

# The master logo artwork (assets/logo-source.png, ~880 KB). It is the INPUT to
# scripts/make_icons.py, which runs on your machine; the served assets it produces live in
# public/ and app/ and are committed. Nothing at build or request time reads the master, so
# it would just be dead weight in the upload.
assets/
__pycache__/
